


Launch & Connect to EC2

Launch an Amazon Linux 2023 or Ubuntu 22.04 instance.

SSH into it:

ssh -i your-key.pem ec2-user@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>

2. Update & Install System Packages

For Amazon Linux:

sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install -y curl python3-pip


For Ubuntu/Debian:

sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y curl python3-pip

3. Set Up Python Virtual Environment
python3 -m venv llm_env
source llm_env/bin/activate

4. Install Python Dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install requests

5. Set Up Mistral API Key

Go to  https://console.mistral.ai
.

Create a new API key.

On EC2, export it:

export MISTRAL_API_KEY="mistral-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"


Confirm it’s set:

echo $MISTRAL_API_KEY


(For persistence, add the line to ~/.bashrc.)

6. Test Mistral API with Curl
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "model": "mistral-tiny",
        "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello from AWS EC2!"}]
      }'


Expected: JSON response with assistant’s reply.

create the file chat_sample.py and run the script and enter the prompts and test

EC2 updated with required tools (python3, pip, curl).

Virtual environment (llm_env) ready.

Dependencies installed (requests).

Mistral API key set and tested via curl.

